  "content_blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": "b00000",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In: Define > Business need",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Overview",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This PPN applies to all central government departments including their executive agencies and non-departmental public bodies (collectively referred to as 'in-scope organisations'). Other contracting authorities (e.g. in local government and wider public sector) may choose to use the guidance set out in this PPN.",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The PPN provides guidance in the form of a decision tree when considering the appropriate choice of procurement route.",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In-scope organisations are also reminded that the general policy expectations for procurement include:",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "use of Lean sourcing principles for all procurements above the relevant Public Contracts Regulations 2015 (PCR 2015) thresholds",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "a strong preference for the Open procedure as the normal default choice for government procurement",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "procurement should not take longer than 120 working days, measured from publication of the contract notice to awarding the contract, except in the case of complex procurements",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "the Restricted procedure should only be used where there is a genuine need to pre-qualify bidders or where there is evidence (following effective pre-market engagement) that the number of potential bidders is very large.",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Objective at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The PPN provides guidance on the choice of procurement route under the PCR 2015 and reminds in-scope organisations of the general policy expectations for procurement.",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Key considerations at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00013",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In-scope organisations should:",
      "ordinal": 13,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00014",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "apply the guidance set out in this PPN (i.e. PPN 12/15) in order to determine an appropriate procurement route",
      "ordinal": 14,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00015",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "have regard to the general policy expectations for procurement.",
      "ordinal": 15,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00016",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Legal framework",
      "ordinal": 16,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00017",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The PPN should be read alongside the relevant parts of the legal framework, including but not limited to, the following provisions of the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 (which may be particularly relevant to the consideration of this PPN):",
      "ordinal": 17,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00018",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 26: Choice of procedures",
      "ordinal": 18,
      "heading_path": [
        "Availability of procurement procedures (decision tree)",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
